Interop harnesses: mimid against Haven's mimi-core and mimi-hubd
(github.com/havenmessenger/interop). Findings are tracked in beads under
mimid-1wgh.46.1, not here. None of this runs in CI: it builds third-party
code and, for the live run, starts servers.

The opposite direction (Haven-encoded messages decoded by mimid) is an
ordinary offline test: crates/mimi-protocol/tests/haven_fixtures.rs.

Layout
  harness/      standalone crate (own [workspace]): Haven's mimi-core, pinned
                to a Haven commit in Cargo.toml, decodes mimid-encoded
                protocol-06 messages, compares fields, re-encodes, and checks
                byte identity. Extra modes: make-kp, make-kp-default (Haven
                mints KeyPackages), decode-commit (Haven decodes a Commit).
  mimid-dump/   zz_dump_for_haven.rs, a mimi-protocol test that writes the
                mimid-encoded messages. It is a template: copy it into
                crates/mimi-protocol/tests/ to run it, then delete it.
  live/         the live run of mimid's PeerClient against mimi-hubd:
    run.sh        builds mimi-hubd from $HAVEN, makes a throwaway CA, and
                  enters an unprivileged user+network namespace (unshare)
    up.sh         (inside) starts mimi-hubd as haven.localhost on
                  127.0.0.1:8443 with mTLS, and socat on haven.localhost:443,
                  which presents a haven.localhost certificate and forwards
                  with the client certificate; sets SSL_CERT_FILE; runs the
                  given command
    selftest.sh   the proxy path works without a client certificate, and the
                  hub refuses direct access
    b4.sh         (inside) seeds Haven over its JSON lane, runs the driver,
                  checks the stored message bytes and the update, and copies
                  mimid's update Commit to out/update_commit.bin
    driver/       standalone crate: mimid crates by relative path, plus a copy
                  of the root Cargo.toml [patch] section (keep the two in step)

Why a namespace and port 443: mimi-hubd builds its directory URLs as
https://{provider_domain}, with no port (havenmessenger/interop#3). The
namespace lets socat own haven.localhost:443 without root.

Requirements: cargo, openssl, socat, unshare with unprivileged user
namespaces, curl.

Variables
  MIMID   this repository's root
  HAVEN   a checkout of github.com/havenmessenger/interop (live run only)
  CACHE   ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}; use private CARGO_TARGET_DIRs
          under it, not a shared target directory

Offline cross-check: mimid encodes, Haven decodes
  export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target
  export MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS=$CACHE/mimid-haven-vectors
  H=$MIMID/tools/interop/haven
  # 1. Haven mints a KeyPackage (diagnostic input)
  (cd $H/harness && cargo run -q -- make-kp $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS)
  # 2. mimid encodes the messages
  cp $H/mimid-dump/zz_dump_for_haven.rs $MIMID/crates/mimi-protocol/tests/
  (cd $MIMID && cargo test -p mimi-protocol --all-features --test zz_dump_for_haven)
  rm $MIMID/crates/mimi-protocol/tests/zz_dump_for_haven.rs
  # 3. Haven decodes them
  (cd $H/harness && cargo run -q -- $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS $MIMID/crates/mimi-mls/tests/fixtures/mlswg)

Live run
  export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-live-target
  (cd $H/live/driver && cargo build)
  # A Haven-minted KeyPackage with openmls's default lifetime and no GREASE
  # (see mimid-1wgh.46.1.13); the test helper's unbounded lifetime is refused
  # by mimid (RFC 9420 section 7.2).
  (cd $H/harness && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target \
     cargo run -q -- make-kp-default $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS)
  cd $H/live
  HAVEN=... ./run.sh ./selftest.sh
  HAVEN=... DRIVER=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/debug/mimid-haven-live \
     KP=$MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS/haven_default_key_package.bin ./run.sh ./b4.sh
  # Haven's own decoder on mimid's update Commit:
  (cd $H/harness && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target \
     cargo run -q -- decode-commit $H/live/out/update_commit.bin)

The driver covers directory, keyMaterial, submitMessage, update and notify.
PeerClient also has requestConsent, updateConsent, identifierQuery and
reportAbuse, which the driver does not exercise yet.

Generated files (vectors, out/, target/) are ignored by git.
